  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="HHFF9F4E3640A578CDF5DE55A091A9A0F9" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium;"&gt;1. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium;" /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium;"&gt;2. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium;" /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium;"&gt;3. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium;" /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium;"&gt;4. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium;" /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: sans-serif; font-size: medium;"&gt;5. Not Applicable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Organization. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;NuStar Logistics L.P. ("NuStar Logistics") is a Delaware limited partnership which wholly owns NuStar Supply &amp;amp; Trading LLC,a Delaware limited liability company, Nustar Permian Holdings, LLC, a Delaware limited liability company and NuStar Finance LLC,a Delaware limited liability company. Nustar also owns 99.99% of NuStar Internacional, S. de R.L. de C.V., a Mexican company. Nustar Logistics is owned 100% by Sunoco LP,a Delaware limited partnership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Operations. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;NuStar Logistics owns pipeline systems and storage terminal assets. The pipelines transport crude oil, refined petroleum products, including gasoline, diesel, and propane throughout Texas, Colorado, New Mexico and Oklahoma.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 12.0pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Undivided Joint Interest. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Nustar Logistics has an undivided joint interest of 50% in the ATA Products Pipeline, 66.67% in El Paso Products Pipeline, and 50% in SAAL Products Pipeline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 12.0pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;. NuStar Logistic's transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") and various state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting practices, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;Basis of Presentation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("GAAP"). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) subsidiaries are reflected on the equity method whereas GAAP requires that all majority-owned subsidiaries be consolidated (2) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and the statement of cash flows and (3) use of FERC approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"&gt;NOTE B - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;"&gt;Accrued capital expenditures as of March 31, 2026 and 2025 were $3 million and $5 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;"&gt;Non-Cash settlements of Investment in Affiliates for the three months ended March 31, 2026 was $5 million.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
